# Valgrind suppressions for RateEngine memory checks.
#
# Only THIRD-PARTY / toolchain false positives belong here - never suppress a
# real RateEngine defect. Keep each entry tightly scoped and commented.

# glibc dynamic linker (ld.so) RPATH/DST handling: is_dst() uses an SSE strncmp
# that reads 8 bytes at a time and over-reads a few bytes past a strdup'd rpath
# token (staying within the mapped page). Harmless, well-known glibc artifact
# triggered by every dlopen() of a module. Not a RateEngine bug.
{
   glibc-ldso-is_dst-rpath-overread-Addr8
   Memcheck:Addr8
   ...
   fun:is_dst
   ...
}

# Same over-read reported as an uninitialised-value/conditional in some glibc
# builds - keep a matching entry so CI is stable across distros.
{
   glibc-ldso-is_dst-rpath-overread-Cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   ...
   fun:is_dst
   ...
}
